WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:05.400
They soared like a plastic meteor straight&nbsp;
into the sun and had a company-wide meltdown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.620
Here's why Funko dumped $30 million of toys&nbsp;
in a landfill, and where they're going next.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:17.040
Funko's humble beginnings date back to 1998, when&nbsp;
toy enthusiast Mike Becker started the business&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:22.320
from his home. For seven years, the company&nbsp;
experienced modest success in selling bobbleheads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.080
including characters such as the Big Boy mascot,&nbsp;
the Cheerios honey bee, Popeye, and others.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:33.240
In 2005, fellow toy enthusiast Brian&nbsp;
Mariotti recognized Funko's potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.240 --> 00:00:38.220
and bought the company from Becker. Shortly&nbsp;
after, Mariotti pivoted slightly away from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:43.260
bobbleheads with a new line of nostalgic-themed&nbsp;
figurines called Fantastik Plastik. Soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.700
Funko began expanding its licensing into&nbsp;
movies, television, and video games,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.060
and showcasing their products&nbsp;
nationwide at different conventions.

00:00:51.060 --> 00:00:54.060
"I think we knew right then and there&nbsp;
that we had something on our hands."

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.260
By 2011, Funko would hit its stride with&nbsp;
a new line of products that would put the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.520
company on a fast track to becoming&nbsp;
a global phenomenon. Cue Funko Pop.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:07.980
Funko's Pop Vinyl line popped up on the&nbsp;
scene as early as 2010, when Brian Mariotti&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:13.860
debuted the prototype at the 2010 San Diego&nbsp;
Comic-Con. Originally named Funko Force 2.0,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.860 --> 00:01:18.180
the line featured characters from the&nbsp;
DC Universe, including Green Lantern,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:23.340
Bat Girl, and two versions of Batman. One year&nbsp;
later, with some slight design adjustments,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.340 --> 00:01:26.640
they were introduced at the New&nbsp;
York Toy Fair as Funko Pops.

00:01:26.640 --> 00:01:31.500
Funko Pops stood out with their large square&nbsp;
heads, disproportionately small bodies, round,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.700
pupilless eyes, and traditionally&nbsp;
no mouth, although certain variants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:40.560
included this feature. Despite their toy-like&nbsp;
appearance, Funko Pop's driving consumers were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:44.820
adults rather than children because, unlike&nbsp;
traditional action figures or bobbleheads,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.820 --> 00:01:50.280
Funko Pop was the first of its kind to offer&nbsp;
something new, leaving no franchise untapped.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:53.400
"It's like a friend that'll never leave&nbsp;
you because you turned into a zombie."

00:01:53.400 --> 00:01:58.860
The Pop line has since expanded to include&nbsp;
other merchandise, such as apparel, plushies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:03.960
and keychains. As time progressed, the Funko&nbsp;
company as a whole only continued to evolve.

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:09.120
A pop culture company like Funko is built on&nbsp;
licensing agreements, which permit Funko to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:14.040
use the licensor's intellectual property. Since&nbsp;
the company's inception, its licenses have grown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:19.140
to include more than 1,000 different properties&nbsp;
from some of the biggest names in pop culture and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:25.200
entertainment. These properties range from movies,&nbsp;
TV, and video games to anime, sports, and music,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:30.780
allowing Funko to produce thousands of characters&nbsp;
— if not tens of thousands — in multiple variants.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:34.080
Although franchises such as "Star&nbsp;
Wars" and "Harry Potter" are some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:37.800
of their best-selling products, Brian&nbsp;
Mariotti assured License Global that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:42.480
Funko wasn't interested in only producing&nbsp;
figures that made the most money. He said:

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.300
"We're going to drive development&nbsp;
based on the characters that mean&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:49.440
the most to us. We want to represent the&nbsp;
brands as best we can, and that doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.740
mean cherry-picking the main characters&nbsp;
and not doing the tertiary characters."

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:56.880
"Is it stupid to have a code, to have honor?"

00:02:56.880 --> 00:02:58.380
"Big words for a little man."

00:02:58.380 --> 00:02:59.040
"Yeah."

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.060
In an era of sequels and remakes&nbsp;
and the luxury of built-in fandoms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:06.360
it seemed only natural that Funko&nbsp;
could stand the test of time.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:13.980
Funko stock went public on November 2, 2017,&nbsp;
setting its IPO at $12 per share, with hopes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.980 --> 00:03:20.400
to raise upwards of $125 million. Their first day&nbsp;
return made headlines, but not for the reasons one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:26.580
would want. Despite pricing lower than expected,&nbsp;
Funko shares dropped 41.1 percent, closing at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:33.720
a meager $7.07. Their stock launch was dubbed the&nbsp;
"worst first-day return for an IPO in 17 years."

00:03:33.720 --> 00:03:39.240
But this bump in the road wasn't enough to deter&nbsp;
the company. Brian Mariotti explained to GeekWire:

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.720
"I told our employees, no matter what&nbsp;
happens, whether the stock goes up,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.720 --> 00:03:46.260
or the stock goes down, it's kind of&nbsp;
irrelevant because we haven't changed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:49.920
anything that we said we are going to do in&nbsp;
the future or what we are currently doing now."

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:51.180
Less than a year later,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.180 --> 00:03:55.970
Funko stock resurged by exceeding its&nbsp;
original $12 pricing. Now that's a pop.

00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:55.980
"Pop pop."

00:03:55.980 --> 00:04:03.600
Business was on the rise. In addition&nbsp;
to selling straight to the consumer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:09.180
Funko expanded to big box retailers as well&nbsp;
as smaller local shops nationwide. In 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:13.980
Funko opened its biggest storefront in Los&nbsp;
Angeles. In their press release, Funko promised,

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.620
"The 40,000-square-foot Hollywood location will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:21.180
be brimming with highly shareable social&nbsp;
media moments, including life-size Funko&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:25.860
statues and immersive 'sets' inspired by&nbsp;
some of the biggest pop culture fandoms."

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:33.120
Funko reached $1 billion in sales in 2021, a 58&nbsp;
percent increase from the year before. But the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:37.200
company wasn't the only thing increasing&nbsp;
in value. Individual Pop figures started&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:41.280
reselling at an all-time high. Retail&nbsp;
prices typically ranged from $10-$15,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:46.380
but if you were lucky enough to get your hands&nbsp;
on certain exclusive or limited edition stock,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.380 --> 00:04:53.220
they could be worth upwards of $25,000. In fact,&nbsp;
Funko Pop's value skyrocketed so much that some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.220 --> 00:04:57.720
even resorted to thievery. Most notably,&nbsp;
a New York City man accidentally knocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.720 --> 00:05:03.240
an elderly woman unconscious while fleeing a&nbsp;
Barnes and Noble with $35 worth of Funko Pops.

00:05:03.240 --> 00:05:06.000
"You know, they're obsessed. It's&nbsp;
a great business you got here."

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:10.140
At this point, many considered their&nbsp;
collections as investments. According&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:15.540
to NASDAQ, the top three most valuable Funko&nbsp;
Pops in 2022 included Alex from "A Clockwork&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:20.760
Orange," Freddy Funko as Venom, and&nbsp;
Metallic Stan Lee. And in May 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:24.600
the largest resale in Funko history&nbsp;
took place in Glendale, California,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:30.300
where a man purchased a rare golden Willy Wonka&nbsp;
set accompanied by a golden ticket for $100,000.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:36.240
As far as Funko Pop consumers go, there are&nbsp;
two types who make up the majority of Funko's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.260
sales. There are the dedicated collectors&nbsp;
who never miss a release and display their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.260 --> 00:05:44.700
vast array of prized possessions for all to&nbsp;
see, and the other is the casual buyer who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.700 --> 00:05:48.900
only picks up specific Funko Pop characters&nbsp;
from their favorite franchises. No matter&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:53.160
which category a consumer falls under, you're no&nbsp;
more or no less a part of the Funko community.

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:58.380
The online community expands further outside&nbsp;
the company, with collectors posting their own&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:03.480
content online centered around Funko. YouTube&nbsp;
creators engage with fellow fans by showcasing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:09.300
their collections, product unboxings, and keeping&nbsp;
subscribers up to date on Funko news. Funko Pop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:13.980
groups sell, trade, and share on Facebook.&nbsp;
But nothing compares to the magic felt when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.980 --> 00:06:18.900
hundreds of Funko fanatics gather in person&nbsp;
at conventions and events. Debuting exclusive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.900 --> 00:06:23.400
lines and interacting with the community&nbsp;
has enabled Funko to carve out a significant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:29.691
space at conventions such as Comic-Con,&nbsp;
Fan Expo, Star Wars Celebration, and E3.

00:06:29.691 --> 00:06:31.361
"Hulkmania is running wild."

00:06:31.361 --> 00:06:31.983
"Brother!"

00:06:31.983 --> 00:06:32.903
"Brother!"

00:06:32.903 --> 00:06:33.947
"Brother!"

00:06:34.631 --> 00:06:35.932
"I can't."

00:06:35.932 --> 00:06:37.860
Although Funko has gained a loyal following,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:41.914
fans aren't afraid to speak up against&nbsp;
unfavorable choices made by the company.

00:06:41.914 --> 00:06:47.220
Take, for example, Funko's venture into&nbsp;
NFTs. In 2021, Funko announced its entry&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:51.840
into the NFT market and was met with a&nbsp;
poor response. As one Reddit user wrote:

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:54.660
"They've shown they don't really&nbsp;
understand the NFT market,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:58.740
and have just seen it as an opportunity to&nbsp;
increase the bottom line, dramatically."

00:06:58.740 --> 00:07:02.280
More criticism followed after&nbsp;
Funko released a Bob Ross NFT,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:07.200
going against the artist's wishes of wanting&nbsp;
to avoid using his likeness for profit.

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:11.340
NFT scandals didn't mark the end&nbsp;
of Funko's controversies. Fans were&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:14.940
surprised when Funko released a dead&nbsp;
Laura Palmer figure from "Twin Peaks."

00:07:14.940 --> 00:07:20.580
A Change.org petition was even created to ban the&nbsp;
character. More recently, Funko came under fire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.580 --> 00:07:25.020
for supposedly whitewashing the character Prince&nbsp;
Naveen from "The Princess and the Frog." The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:29.400
company Twitter account deleted the original image&nbsp;
and released a follow-up statement which said:

00:07:29.400 --> 00:07:32.520
"Our previous post showed an&nbsp;
image of the Naveen Funko Pop!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.520 --> 00:07:35.760
that is not true to the product,&nbsp;
which is accurately shown here."

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.760
Still, this wouldn't be the&nbsp;
company's first offense in this area,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:38.760 --> 00:07:42.720
with similar accusations leveled at&nbsp;
it in the past. These controversies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:45.540
combined have been enough to cause&nbsp;
some distrust in the company.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:50.940
What was once considered a key selling point&nbsp;
for Funko became its greatest flaw. As far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:54.780
as Funko is concerned, the company is in the&nbsp;
business of creating something for everyone.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.280
Not only are there thousands of characters to&nbsp;
choose from, but there's also a long list of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:03.600
variants for each character. Chase variants&nbsp;
offer an alternative version of a character,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.600 --> 00:08:07.980
including anything from an outfit change&nbsp;
to a glow-in-the-dark appearance. Flocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.980 --> 00:08:12.000
variants replace the vinyl texture with&nbsp;
a soft, fuzzy one. Diamond variants add&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.000 --> 00:08:15.900
a shimmer of glitter to characters. The&nbsp;
list continues with chrome, metallic,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:15.900 --> 00:08:21.660
and black light variants. Comedian and television&nbsp;
host Conan O'Brien had 34 variants alone.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:24.960
"Yeah, otherwise known as Conan&nbsp;
without coffee and makeup."

00:08:24.960 --> 00:08:29.940
Perhaps it became too much. When Funko's&nbsp;
third quarter report for 2022 was released,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.940 --> 00:08:33.300
the company revealed that there&nbsp;
was an issue involving a surplus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:38.040
in inventory. To make matters worse, chains&nbsp;
were delaying or canceling orders. Overall,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.040 --> 00:08:44.160
the third quarter of 2022 reported a 39 percent&nbsp;
decline in net income from the previous year. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:48.060
an attempt to push out more supply, more&nbsp;
and more Funko products began popping up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:52.380
in discount stores and hitting clearance&nbsp;
shelves. Still, the worst was yet to come.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:57.120
Funko's fourth quarter report for&nbsp;
2022 proved just how detrimental the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.120 --> 00:09:00.300
damage had become. Brian Mariotti&nbsp;
revealed in a conference call:

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.440
"A combination of macro factors&nbsp;
and Funko-specific issues have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:08.520
disrupted our financial and operating&nbsp;
performance to an unacceptable degree."

00:09:08.520 --> 00:09:12.960
One of these factors was the exponential&nbsp;
cost of housing excess inventory. Part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:15.120
of the company's solution made shocking headlines:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:19.020
since attempting to sell off the inventory&nbsp;
at a discounted price wasn't cutting it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:19.020 --> 00:09:24.420
Funko instead made the decision to dump at least&nbsp;
$30 million worth of product into a landfill.

00:09:24.420 --> 00:09:25.860
"So where are we now?"

00:09:26.760 --> 00:09:28.320
"In the garbage truck on the way to the dump."

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:38.160
Between the waste, environmental concerns, and&nbsp;
inconsideration with regards to this decision,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:42.540
fans of Funko were disappointed, to&nbsp;
say the least. One Reddit user said:

00:09:42.540 --> 00:09:45.840
"This is most likely just another&nbsp;
example of corporate greed. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:49.620
would rather throw unsold merchandise&nbsp;
away than donate it or give it away."

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:52.740
But is bad press enough to&nbsp;
tank the company for good?

00:09:52.740 --> 00:09:57.420
While all this was going on, Funko's stock&nbsp;
continued to drop after a drastic fall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.420 --> 00:10:03.960
following 2022's third quarter earnings. NASDAQ&nbsp;
reported that the stock dropped a whopping 59.3&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.960 --> 00:10:08.340
percent. Funko's downfall became a numbers&nbsp;
game, with the company on the losing end.

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:10.140
"It's extra surprising, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.140 --> 00:10:13.500
given that Funko reported better than&nbsp;
expected revenue in the latest quarter."

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:18.960
Comparing 2021 and 2022's fourth quarter&nbsp;
reports, net sales decreased by one percent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:24.060
while net income decreased by a&nbsp;
staggering 368 percent. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:27.180
the company kept up an optimistic&nbsp;
front, writing in the report,

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:32.400
"Funko is highly focused on identifying and&nbsp;
addressing opportunities for improvement. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:36.600
these initiatives will take several&nbsp;
quarters in some cases, and as a result,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.740
we expect sequential improvement throughout&nbsp;
the year as our initiatives take hold."

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:46.320
What exactly does all this mean for the future of&nbsp;
Funko? Many factors come into play when analyzing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.320 --> 00:10:51.240
what went wrong between 2021's record-breaking&nbsp;
profits and the shortcomings of the second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:51.240 --> 00:10:56.760
half of 2022. When comparing Funko to other&nbsp;
collectibles that eventually faded into obscurity,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:02.040
such as Beanie Babies, the pattern becomes&nbsp;
more clear. Commonality and similarity are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.040 --> 00:11:07.860
slowly hurting Funko's collectible brand. As Funko&nbsp;
tries to cater to everyone by creating Funko Pops&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:12.960
for everything under the pop culture sun, the only&nbsp;
value comes from consumers buying at retail price.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:17.520
During the height of the COVID pandemic, people&nbsp;
clung to entertainment and hobbies for comfort.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.520 --> 00:11:23.040
Funko products weren't exactly new, but their&nbsp;
virality drew in an excited new crowd. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:27.720
as time went on, that excitement diminished&nbsp;
slightly. Of course, this doesn't mean no one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:32.640
is buying Funko products. There was still a 29&nbsp;
percent increase in net sales for the full fiscal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:39.360
year of 2022, compared to 2021. So if Funko can&nbsp;
sort out its supply issues and bring a new level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:43.560
of excitement back to the collector community,&nbsp;
there could still be hope for the future.

